aken from other generated frames, aligned and feathered.","src":{"yaw":"jena-r5-yaw-atlas.mp4 (Kling 2.5 turbo pro i2v)","yawB":"jena-r5-yaw-atlas-B.mp4 (Kling 2.5 turbo pro i2v)","talk":"jena-r5-talk.mp4 (Veo 3.1 fast i2v)","talkB":"jena-r5-talk-B.mp4 (Veo 3.1 fast i2v)","talkC":"jena-c18-talk.mp4 (Veo 3.1 fast i2v, camfix18, frames 1-56 only)"},"camfix19":"dropped: every yawB frame (head-tilted sly/half-lidded grin), yaw rig frames 48-146 (profile eye lowered / side-eye, then head-down look-up smirk), old talkB/talkC full frames (wide/manic eyes, washed 3D style), old blinkgen (55% crossfade frames read as a wink). Added: 8 blink composites (both eyes shut, eye area from old blinkgen frame 355), 120 talk composites = 15 mouth shapes (mouth/jaw from camfix18 rig frames [310, 334, 315, 316, 311, 313, 314, 317, 312, 318, 329, 330, 331, 332, 333], 4 loudness levels) x 8 rest bases; eyes are always the rest frame calm happy eyes.","camfix20":"camfix20 uses the camfix19 rig unchanged (all 176 frames re-viewed by eye by camfix20: both eyes open in every rest/turn frame, both eyes shut in every blink frame, calm rest eyes in all 120 talk composites).","turnfix1":"2026-10-26 turnfix1: all 40 old turn frames 8-47 (real frames of the generated head-turn video) showed a closed-teeth / clenched side grin (frames 41-47 also narrowed eyes) and were replaced in place. New frames 8-47 are rest frame 0 (the big open IMG_3647 smile, both eyes open) warped in 2D: a smooth ellipsoid head-yaw warp easing 0->16 deg toward the viewer's left plus 0->2.2 deg head tilt, body fixed. No new generation, $0. Honest label: 2.5D, a 2D warp of one approved frame, not a 3D model. Pairs now link every rest frame 0-7 to turn frame 8 (frame 8 = rest frame 0 exactly) with a zero flow, so entering a turn is a 2-tick crossfade between near-identical rest frames. Blink and talk frames 48-175 unchanged."}}